    Identity management extends core's existing System: Authentication Servers
    privilege. Core's default pluggable ACL merge replaces duplicate identifiers, so
    ACL.php deliberately appends this API pattern instead.

    Discovery reads a provider document so an exact issuer can be checked while it is
    being typed. It makes this firewall fetch an address somebody chose, which is why it
    is a privilege of its own. Provider setup is separate too: it performs no network
    request, but only a delegated server administrator should generate security
    configuration intended for another system. The read-only health endpoint
    extends the existing authentication-server privilege and reveals only cache
    states and timestamps. The sign-in test starts the same
    provider redirect as a login, but only after an authenticated, CSRF-protected
    request and without granting a local session at its callback.

    The endpoints under api/openidconnect/auth/ are deliberately NOT listed. They answer before
    anyone is signed in and decline the session check themselves; what protects them is
    the state and the nonce this firewall issued, not a privilege.

    Without this file these endpoints are reachable by administrators alone, because
    core denies a page no ACL entry matches. That works, but it leaves most of the rule
    implicit and nowhere to be seen under System > Access > Groups.
-->
<acl>
    <page-system-openidconnect-discovery>
        <name>System: Access: Servers: OpenID Connect discovery</name>
        <patterns>
            <pattern>api/openidconnect/discovery/*</pattern>
        </patterns>
    </page-system-openidconnect-discovery>
    <page-system-openidconnect-setup>
        <name>System: Access: Servers: OpenID Connect provider setup</name>
        <patterns>
            <pattern>api/openidconnect/setup/*</pattern>
        </patterns>
    </page-system-openidconnect-setup>
    <page-system-openidconnect-test>
        <name>System: Access: Servers: OpenID Connect sign-in test</name>
        <patterns>
            <pattern>api/openidconnect/test/*</pattern>
        </patterns>
    </page-system-openidconnect-test>
    <page-system-authservers>
        <name>System: Authentication Servers</name>
        <patterns>
            <pattern>api/openidconnect/approval/*</pattern>
            <pattern>api/openidconnect/health/*</pattern>
        </patterns>
    </page-system-authservers>
</acl>
